  "id": "Compound::DB00306 - Gene::2562",
  "verbalization": "Talbutal is implicated in the relationship with Gabrb3 through a series of interconnected molecular and functional pathways. The evidence suggests that Talbutal binds to Chrna7, which is involved in transmitter-gated channel activity, and this activity is linked to Gabrb3. Similarly, Talbutal binds to Gabrb1, which participates in Gaba receptor activity, and this activity is also linked to Gabrb3. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Talbutal influences Gaba receptor function, ultimately affecting Gabrb3. The consistent involvement of Gaba receptor activity in both pathways underscores a shared functional role in the target system. The evidence supports a mechanism where Talbutal modulates Gaba receptor activity through different binding sites, leading to a potential effect on Gabrb3. The integration of these pathways suggests that Talbutal may act through a GABAergic pathway to influence Gabrb3, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
